div.p:
A person's kind is its type, from a vocabulary of the application that grows, which these seed:
      historical, a person of the texts' times, the default, which needn't be written;
      modernScholar, an author or editor of a publication; divine, God, Christ, the Spirit;
      fictitious, a name a text takes, such as Isidorus Mercator, the name Pseudo-Isidore's preface gives
      its compiler. A type outside them is reported, so that a slip is seen and a new type is added on purpose. Made
      up:
